ted (controller, auto_queue, extract dispatch/process, file_operation_manager, model_builder, web stream_model/serialize_model, and tests) are unaffected.","Import safety: common/__init__.py line 1 re-exports sanitize_log_value from .types. model.py already imported AppError from common, so this adds no new import cycle or package dependency.","Type safety: the helper calls value.replace(...), so it needs a str. file.name is a ModelFile name (str), and remove_file(filename) is keyed by the same str names used in self.__files. If a caller passed a non-str name it would already fail the dict lookup semantics. No new crash path was found.","Behavior change visible to operators: DEBUG log lines for filenames that contain control characters now show escaped tokens (\\n, \\r, \\xHH) instead of the raw bytes. Any log grep or alerting that matched raw control characters in these three DEBUG lines would change, which is unlikely and only at DEBUG level. C1 and non-ASCII Unicode filenames pass through unchanged, so normal international filenames look the same.","Schema/DB/migration: none. Model state is in memory only, and nothing is persisted or serialized differently. serialize_model and stream_model read ModelFile objects, not log output.","Blast radius: limited to the text of 3 DEBUG log lines in one module. If the helper had a bug, the worst case would be an exception raised inside add/remove/update before the model mutates. That would affect the controller scan loop, but the helper is simple, pure and already tested by its existing callers.","Verdict: shippable as-is. No blocking issues; the only finding is a negligible performance note."]}
